1. Purpose

This license permits limited use of the Software for evaluation, development, testing, research, education, and other non-production purposes.

Any Production Use of the Software requires a separate paid commercial license from Zyvor AI Labs Private Limited ("Zyvor").

By downloading, installing, accessing, modifying, compiling, or otherwise using the Software, you agree to the terms of this license.

2. Definitions

2.1 Software

"Software" means the source code, object code, binaries, documentation, configuration files, scripts, APIs, SDKs, agents, controllers, user interfaces, and other materials distributed under this license.

2.2 Non-Production Use

"Non-Production Use" means use solely for:

* evaluation;
* proof-of-concept testing;
* software development;
* internal testing;
* quality assurance;
* laboratory environments;
* demonstrations;
* research;
* education; or
* personal experimentation.

Non-Production Use must not support live business operations, customers, revenue-generating services, or production workloads.

2.3 Production Use

"Production Use" means any deployment or use of the Software that:

* supports live business operations;
* protects, monitors, manages, processes, routes, stores, or serves production data or workloads;
* is used by employees, contractors, customers, partners, or end users as part of normal business operations;
* is deployed on production servers, production clusters, production networks, production edge devices, or customer environments;
* is used to provide a commercial product or service;
* generates or supports revenue;
* is incorporated into an OEM product, appliance, platform, managed service, SaaS offering, or hosted service;
* is used for business continuity, security, observability, networking, infrastructure management, automation, orchestration, or operational decision-making in a live environment.

Production Use requires a valid paid commercial license issued by Zyvor.

2.4 Organization

"Organization" means a company, partnership, institution, government body, or other legal entity, together with its affiliates, subsidiaries, and any entity under common control, and any individual acting for or on behalf of any of them.

2.5 Evaluation Period

"Evaluation Period" means 30 days, counted from the first day on which any person in an Organization first installs, runs, or accesses a given Software product, and counted cumulatively across all machines, environments, accounts, versions, and reinstallations. The Evaluation Period applies once per Organization per Software product and is not restarted by upgrading, reinstalling, re-cloning, or moving the Software.

3. Free License Grant

Subject to compliance with this license, Zyvor grants you a limited, worldwide, non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable, royalty-free license to:

* download the Software;
* inspect the source code;
* compile and run the Software;
* modify the Software for internal evaluation;
* test integrations;
* perform proof-of-concept deployments; and
* use the Software for Non-Production Use.

No rights for Production Use are granted under this free license.

The free license for an Organization is limited to the Evaluation Period. After the Evaluation Period ends, an Organization must stop all use of the Software and delete all copies unless it holds a valid written commercial license or a written extension signed by Zyvor. An extension is effective only if it is in writing, identifies the Organization and the Software product, and states an end date.

An individual who is not acting for or on behalf of an Organization may use the Software for personal learning, personal experimentation, and non-commercial education without the Evaluation Period limit, but only for Non-Production Use.

