15. No Circumvention

You may not intentionally circumvent restrictions imposed by this license by:

* splitting one production deployment into multiple evaluation environments;
* repeatedly reinstalling trial versions;
* using multiple organizations or accounts to avoid licensing limits;
* operating production workloads under labels such as "testing", "development", or "evaluation";
* cloning or modifying the Software primarily to avoid payment obligations.

The actual nature and purpose of the deployment determines whether it constitutes Production Use.

Use is presumed to be Production Use, unless you show otherwise by written records, if:

* it continues after the Evaluation Period ends without a valid commercial license or written extension;
* it processes real customer, employee, financial, or operational data;
* it is reachable by anyone outside the team evaluating the Software; or
* it runs on infrastructure that also runs production workloads.

Use by affiliates, subsidiaries, contractors, or related parties to obtain a second Evaluation Period, or to avoid a limit, a fee, or the Evaluation Period, is treated as use by the same Organization.

