Free, for a limited time

An Organization may use the Software without payment for 30 days per Software product (the Evaluation Period) for:

* development;
* testing;
* evaluation;
* proofs of concept;
* research;
* education; and
* non-production laboratory environments.

After 30 days an Organization must stop using the Software unless it holds a commercial license or a written extension from Zyvor. Individuals acting for themselves, and not for an Organization, may continue personal, non-commercial learning and experimentation.

Paid License Required

A commercial license is required for:

* production environments;
* customer workloads;
* internal business-critical workloads;
* commercial services;
* SaaS;
* managed services;
* OEM use;
* appliances;
* redistribution;
* resale;
* revenue-generating use; and
* enterprise production deployments.

Production = Commercial License Required. Unlicensed Production Use is billed at list price from the first day plus a further 100%, with interest and costs, and may also lead to criminal complaints, fines, and imprisonment under applicable law.

